I too got bored with becoming invincible to all but insta-deaths
(ITABI?) by the time I made it to the Valley of Death, if not well
before.  Also with my characters gathering essentially the same kit
regardless of race/class (I had ascended all races and most classes).
And the idea of voluntarily avoiding useful behavior as a challenge
didn't appeal to me much, although I tried some and succeeded a few.

So I moved to SlashEM, which I had consciously avoided and denigrated
previously.  However, monsters and their improved physical and more
varied special attacks maintain a real threat of death by HP loss as
far as I've progressed.  While some of the added artifacts are
frivolous, others (and added non-artifact magical items as well) give a
real choice on different ways to kit up.  There are more special levels
with bosses which can be challenging for the level they appear on.  All
the named demons appear in Gehennom, which is shorter as well (I think,
as I don't have much experience in Gehennom in SlashEM).

So for what it's worth, switching to SlashEM has been an effective and
lasting cure to the boredom that had set in for me on vanilla Nethack
as well.  I don't think I've played one game of vanilla since I
switched.  Maybe when a new version comes out.

